ps://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's technically possible in C++\r\n* open https://www.w3schools.com/cpp/trycpp.asp?filename=demo_enum_access\r\n* replace `enum Level myVar = MEDIUM;` with `Level myVar = (Level)13;`\r\n* run. prints `13`\r\n\r\nI want to test (this weekend) it by removing the mapping for my controller and then checking the outputs. Can be tested w/o a custom build. Just \"hoping\" that my joypad's technical numbers are \"out of range\" to verify this","created_at":"2024-11-16T12:07:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-16T12:07:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1844965977","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1844965977"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1844965977"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1844965977/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":null,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1844964333,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845385019","pull_request_review_id":2440938145,"id":1845385019,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5t_lc7","diff_hunk":"@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@\n \t<members>\n \t\t<member name=\"button_index\" type=\"int\" setter=\"set_button_index\" getter=\"get_button_index\" enum=\"JoyButton\" default=\"0\">\n \t\t\tButton identifier. One of the [enum JoyButton] button constants.\n+\t\t\tFor unmapped joypads, this identifier does not necessarily match the [enum JoyButton] button constants. To check if your device is mapped, use [method Input.is_joy_known].","path":"doc/classes/InputEventJoypadButton.xml","commit_id":"6c9354fa1ea904a5f98bc7536138ad0d952fc6be","original_commit_id":"19c7ffff0d61b50e63805daaa9dcb05e618e8375","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ok, I could test on Linux, and it doesn't go out-of-range. But that is only because the indices start at 0, and are manually incremented. And the technical max number is 767 (as taken from the Linux kernel code). And I have no controller with that many buttons. So yeah, it could happen there, if you have a controller with enough buttons.  \r\nBut the button index order did change for unmapped joypads, as expected, so the \"JoyButton\" has basically no reliability for those.\r\n\r\nIt seems this out-of-range issue is somewhat expected looking at some code, such as [`InputEventJoypadButton::as_text`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.3/core/input/input_event.cpp#L1284). Or it was a \"just in case\" safety implementation, who knows.\r\n\r\nOn iOS and macOS, it seems they hard-coded to use JoyButton and JoyAxis. So that's safe.\r\n\r\nOn Web, it seems they clamp it at 16 buttons and 10 axes (in `godot_js_input_gamepad_sample_get`). So that's safe as well.\r\n\r\nOn Android, there's `getGodotButton`, where `default` could result in any button index of value `getMaxKeyCode` (is 318 atm) - 168.\r\n\r\nOn Windows, it's clamped to 17 buttons for XInput (even though there are only 14 supported according to the docs, [I made a PR to fix that](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99313), though I'm curious to check it out, because XInput officially does not seem to support the GUIDE button), and 128 for DirectInput.  \r\n\r\nSo, I'll test soon on Windows for XInput devices (I have no DirectInput device), and then I reckon I'll update the class docs and give some info per target platform.\r\n\r\nAnd I think I'll hard-code some fake high button index and test GDScript on Linux and see what happens. I expect nothing, because the binding for the property is `int`: `ADD_PROPERTY(PropertyInfo(Variant::INT, \"button_index\"), \"set_button_index\", \"get_button_index\");`","created_at":"2024-11-17T10:08:25Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T10:16:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1845385019","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845385019"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1845385019"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845385019/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":null,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1844964333,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845466735","pull_request_review_id":2441033417,"id":1845466735,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5t_5Zv","diff_hunk":"@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@\n \t<members>\n \t\t<member name=\"button_index\" type=\"int\" setter=\"set_button_index\" getter=\"get_button_index\" enum=\"JoyButton\" default=\"0\">\n \t\t\tButton identifier. One of the [enum JoyButton] button constants.\n+\t\t\tFor unmapped joypads, this identifier does not necessarily match the [enum JoyButton] button constants. To check if your device is mapped, use [method Input.is_joy_known].","path":"doc/classes/InputEventJoypadButton.xml","commit_id":"6c9354fa1ea904a5f98bc7536138ad0d952fc6be","original_commit_id":"19c7ffff0d61b50e63805daaa9dcb05e618e8375","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"OK, I overlooked `ERR_FAIL_INDEX((int)p_button, (int)JoyButton::MAX);` in `Input::joy_button`, so Godot will catch technical button indices that are out-of-range.\r\n\r\nThe problem is: you _can_ map joypads with more than 128 buttons, but then `Input::joy_button` throws them away. Affected are Android and Linux. I guess I'll make a warning print in the mapping func (in this PR)","created_at":"2024-11-17T13:36:08Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T13:37:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1845466735","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845466735"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99314#discussion_r1845466735"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99314"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1845466735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":null,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1844964333,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2709495359","pull_request_review_id":3683579259,"id":2709495359,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6hf54_","diff_hunk":"@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ enum class JoyButton {\n \tPADDLE4 = 19,\n \tTOUCHPAD = 20,\n \tSDL_MAX = 21,\n-\tMAX = 128, // Android supports up to 36 buttons. DirectInput supports up to 128 buttons.\n+\tMAX = 128, // DirectX supports up to 14 buttons